page_head #= language_theme_head

#[navbar]

#[section, $md:
    @../ (Documentation) / Design scope

    # Design scope

    Moth admits a feature only when it fits the language's small, explicit
    source model. Features marked deferred belong to that model but still await
    implementation. Features outside scope conflict with it.

    This distinction prevents an unsupported feature from looking like a design
    promise, and it explains why Moth chooses constrained templates, choices and
    static traits over broader mechanisms found in other languages.
]

